        "AbstractText": "We present the case of a 67 year-old patient that presented to our institution with acute and severe chest pain. Optical coherence tomography high-resolution images of the coronary lumen, allowed us to confirm diagnosis of spontaneous coronary artery dissection, guide treatment, and verify the results of our intervention."
